    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d476">

                <pb facs="0593" n="583" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg583"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.002/11–1748: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-17T17:00:00+08:00">November 17,
                            1948—5 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:52 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2242. Hu Shih<anchor n="21" xml:id="d476-f1"/> told me yesterday that he is
                    prepared to accept premiership of National Government if three conditions are
                    fulfilled: (1) that US President or Secretary State make public statement of
                    moral support of National Government; (2) that American economic <pb facs="0594"
                        n="584" xml:id="pg584"/> and military assistance be stepped up; (3) that he
                    be given free hand to pick his own Cabinet.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, pouched Peiping.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d476-f1" n="21" xml:id="d476-f1-content">
                <p>Chancellor of the National Peking University.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
